{"diksanKye sanjYayam‌": [{"id": "diksaMKye saMjYAyAm‌", "headword": "दिक्संख्ये संज्ञायाम्‌", "headword_slp1": "diksaMKye saMjYAyAm‌", "fold": "diksanKye sanjYayam‌", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The words expressing a point of the compass or a number (संख्या ) enter into compostion with the word correlated to them by being in the same case, when the sense of the compound is that of an appellative and the resulting compound is तत्-पुरुष ।\n\nTerms: समास-तत्-पुरुष", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दिक्संख्ये संज्ञायाम्‌ २.१.५०", "२.१.५०", "२.१.५० दिक्संख्ये संज्ञायाम्‌"], "synonyms_slp1": ["diksaMKye saMjYAyAm‌ २.१.५०", "२.१.५०", "२.१.५० diksaMKye saMjYAyAm‌"]}], "dikpurvapadanNip‌": [{"id": "dikpUrvapadAnNIp‌", "headword": "दिक्पूर्वपदान्ङीप्‌", "headword_slp1": "dikpUrvapadAnNIp‌", "fold": "dikpurvapadanNip‌", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The feminine affix ङीप् comes after a प्रातिपदिक (Nominal Stem) which is preceded by a word signifying direction.\n\nTerms: विभक्ति-ङीप्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दिक्पूर्वपदान्ङीप्‌ ४.१.६०", "४.१.६०", "४.१.६० दिक्पूर्वपदान्ङीप्‌"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dikpUrvapadAnNIp‌ ४.१.६०", "४.१.६०", "४.१.६० dikpUrvapadAnNIp‌"]}], "dikpurvapadadasanjYayan YaH": [{"id": "dikpUrvapadAdasaMjYAyAM YaH", "headword": "दिक्पूर्वपदादसंज्ञायां ञः", "headword_slp1": "dikpUrvapadAdasaMjYAyAM YaH", "fold": "dikpurvapadadasanjYayan YaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix ञ comes in the remaining senses after a word preceded by another that signifies 'direction' provided the compound is not a name.\n\nTerms: ञ", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["दिक्पूर्वपदादसंज्ञायां ञः ४.२.१०७", "४.२.१०७", "४.२.१०७ दिक्पूर्वपदादसंज्ञायां ञः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["dikpUrvapadAdasaMjYAyAM YaH ४.२.१०७", "४.२.१०७", "४.२.१०७ dikpUrvapadAdasaMjYAyAM YaH"]}], "dikpurvapadawWaY ca": [{"id"